Subject: [PATCH 3/4] RISC-V: Implement scheduling for ARC-V RHX-100 series.

This patch implements instruction scheduling support for the dual-issue
ARC-V RHX-100 processor by adding scheduler hooks and state tracking for
the two execution pipes.

These hooks address microarchitectural details not covered by the
pipeline description.

The riscv_sched_variable_issue () and riscv_sched_reorder2 () hooks work
together to make sure that:
  - the critical path and the instruction priorities are respected;
  - both pipes are filled (taking advantage of parallel dispatch within
    the microarchitectural constraints);
  - there is as much fusion going on as possible;
  - the existing fusion pairs are not broken up.

riscv_sched_adjust_priority () slightly bumps the priority of load/store
pairs.  As a result it becomes easier for riscv_sched_reorder2 () to
schedule instructions in the memory pipe.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/riscv/arcv.cc (struct arcv_sched_state): New.
	(arcv_sched_init, arcv_sched_reorder2, arcv_sched_adjust_priority,
	arcv_sched_adjust_cost, arcv_can_issue_more_p,
	arcv_sched_variable_issue): New.
	* config/riscv/riscv-protos.h: Declare them.
	* config/riscv/riscv.cc (riscv_sched_init): Call arcv_sched_init.
	(riscv_sched_variable_issue, riscv_sched_adjust_cost): Handle RHX-100.
	(riscv_sched_adjust_priority, riscv_sched_reorder2): New.
	(TARGET_SCHED_ADJUST_PRIORITY, TARGET_SCHED_REORDER2): Define.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/riscv/fusion-ls-update.c: Remove XFAIL.
	* gcc.target/riscv/fusion-ls-update-2.c: Likewise, and fix the
	scan pattern.

